irement:req-2b2b91a584].", "entry": "axil_timer"}, {"path": "tb/axil_timer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axil_timer self-checking testbench (ADDR_WIDTH 4, 5, 8)", "summary": "Top axil_timer_tb instantiates a test core at ADDR_WIDTH 4, 5 and 8, each with its own DUT and clock. Each core checks against [artifact:prj-ada3a9b9d9.interface-spec.a2], with edge-exact timing derived from a cycle counter. It covers:\n- reset values;\n- byte strobes and CTRL/STATUS write rules;\n- COUNT and unmapped writes answering SLVERR, with no aliasing;\n- AW/W in either order, B and R stalls with stable responses, and the READY equations;\n- read/write on the same edge;\n- one-shot and periodic counting (COUNT read at every k);\n- LOAD 0 and LOAD 1;\n- restart, stop and CTRL-on-end-edge cases, and END-BEATS-CLEAR;\n- irq edges and 32-bit borrow;\n- both TMR-LOAD-END-EDGE outcomes;\n- reset dropping held AW, held W and pending B/R.\n\nFailures report through $error. The testbench counts passes and prints a single NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line. Traces to [requirement:req-2b2b91a584].", "entry": "axil_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["I have not run lint, simulation, synthesis or any formal tool on these files. Whether they are lint-clean, pass simulation or synthesize without latches is unknown until the platform runs lint.run, simulator.run and synth.run.", "The expected values in the testbench come from my own reading of the interface spec. The same reader wrote the RTL, so a shared misreading would not be caught. Independent review is required (P6).", "The testbench uses $error. It assumes the platform's Icarus invocation accepts $error. Some Icarus language-generation settings may not.", "The `ifdef FORMAL` assertions are design intent only and have not been proven. No formal_spec is submitted, so formal.run and formal.cover do not apply.", "Interface open item I1 (the 'bits 31:21' wording in TMR-COUNT) is still unresolved with the customer. The RTL uses full 32-bit end det